  "final_message": "I have launched the test command and am waiting for the baseline test suite to complete.\nWaiting for `npm test` to finish.\nI will wait for git status to finish.\nI will wait for the directory listing.\nI will wait for the analytics-ingest test suite to complete.\nWaiting for `analytics-ingest` tests.\nI will wait for the search to complete.\nWaiting for task.\nI will wait for git log to finish.\nI will wait for the environment check to complete.\nI will wait for git status to complete.\nRemoving `channel` from the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/orders-service/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event would break downstream consumers.\n\n### Why `channel` Cannot Be Removed Yet\n\nWhile `billing-service` and `web-storefront` do not consume `channel`, **`analytics-ingest` (Team Data)** actively depends on it:\n\n1. **Explicit Contract**: In [`analytics-ingest/README.md`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/analytics-ingest/README.md#L26-L32), the contract with `orders-service` requires `channel` (`web | store | marketplace`).\n2. **Schema Validation**: In [`decodeOrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts#L416-L437), `analytics-ingest` strictly validates `channel`:\n   ```ts\n   const channel = reader.oneOf(\"channel\", CHANNELS);\n   ```\n3. **Data Lake Persistence**: In [`toOrderRow`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/analytics-ingest/src/ingest.ts#L693-L701), `channel` is populated directly into the `orders` lake table.\n4. **Failing Loudly**: A missing `channel` throws a [`ContractViolationError`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/analytics-ingest/src/core/errors.ts#L368-L377) and discards the event completely (tested in [`ingest.test.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/analytics-ingest/test/ingest.test.ts#L88-L90)).\n\n### Recommended Next Steps\n\nBecause other team repositories are checked out read-only, changes cannot be made directly to `analytics-ingest`. To safely decommission `channel`:\n\n1. **Coordinate with Team Data**: Update `analytics-ingest` to make `channel` optional (or stop reading it) and deploy that change.\n2. **Deprecate or Version the Event**: If breaking changes are needed, introduce a new schema version (e.g. `schemaVersion: 4`) following the event versioning strategy.\n3. **Remove from `orders-service`**: Once no downstream consumers require `channel`, remove it from the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/orders-service/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) domain model and [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/orders-service/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event.\nThe working directory is clean and all tests across both [`orders-service`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/orders-service) and [`analytics-ingest`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/analytics-ingest) remain passing. Please let me know how you'd like to proceed with coordinating this migration.\n",
